# R42 tail-reserve boundary cell.
#
# break-only-if-it-NARROWS · the SUPPRESSED half. A ONE-ITEM list whose open
# delimiter sits at or LEFT of its own continuation column: `    f(` puts the
# packer at column 6 while the continuation column is 8. Breaking would move
# the item to the RIGHT, buying a second line that is WIDER than the one it
# replaced — the break narrows nothing, so it is not spent.
#
# ZERO corpus instances: this cell's evidence is this fixture.
#
# RED, recorded against the PRE-FIX binary built from this track's own base
# commit: it emits TWO lines — `    f(` (6) plus a 147-column continuation.
# GREEN: ONE line of 145 columns. Still over budget (the string is an
# unbreakable atom and no formatter can fix that), but strictly narrower than
# the shape the break produced, and one line instead of two.
#
# The overrun below is the DOCTRINAL unbreakable-atom escape, not a defect.

void f(String s):
    print(s)

void main():
    f("aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa")
